abstract: >-
  data-gravity-operator is a Kubernetes operator that implements
  data-locality-aware workload scheduling for distributed physics data
  lakes modelled on the Worldwide LHC Computing Grid (WLCG) and the
  Rucio data-management system. It introduces a PhysicsJob custom
  resource: when a user submits a PhysicsJob referencing a Rucio
  dataset identifier (DID), the operator resolves the dataset's
  primary Rucio Storage Element (RSE), maps that RSE to a Kubernetes
  node via the topology.cern.io/site label, and creates an owned
  batch/v1.Job with NodeAffinity constraints injected so compute runs
  co-located with the data. This avoids inter-site WAN transfers that
  the standard kube-scheduler would otherwise incur.
